node_modules/
dist/
build/
# ── Environment files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DENY-BY-DEFAULT. This was previously a hand-maintained list
# (.env, .env.local, .env.production) which did not cover new variants — that
# gap is how server/.env.development reached a public commit (6dc972b)
# carrying a live MongoDB Atlas credential.
#
# A wildcard cannot have that gap. `.env*` has no slash, so git applies it at
# EVERY depth — it catches .env.staging, and also a typo'd `.envlocal`
# (already present in this repo) that a `.env.*` rule would miss.
#
# Templates are committed deliberately, so they are explicitly un-ignored.
# `.env*.example` covers .env.example and .env.local.example at any depth.
# If you add another template convention, whitelist it here — never loosen
# the deny rule above it.
.env*
!.env*.example
!.env*.sample
!.env*.template
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
coverage/
deploy/certs/
deploy/certbot-www/

# Checkpoint gate output (tools/checkpoint-gate)
gate-report/
